1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,307
What if every component derivative is correct, yet the
engineering decision is wrong?

2
00:00:05,307 --> 00:00:09,718
Coldplate asks where a limited amount of metal should go
in a buoyancy-cooled chip.

3
00:00:09,718 --> 00:00:15,314
At strong coupling, cutting one feedback loop changes
which cells we choose and how much cooling we realize.

4
00:00:15,564 --> 00:00:21,973
The pipeline serves a PyTorch material map, a C plus plus
Eigen flow solver, and a thermal solver.

5
00:00:21,973 --> 00:00:28,150
Temperature drives buoyancy; velocity advects heat, so the
converged state is a two-way fixed point.

6
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:35,522
Newton Krylov crosses the component boundary with J V P's;
the implicit adjoint crosses it again with V J P's.

7
00:00:35,522 --> 00:00:45,448
The thermal slot swaps JAX autodiff for independent
Fortran differentiated by Enzyme at LLVM I R, and the full
coupled pipeline is checked again after the swap.

8
00:00:45,698 --> 00:00:51,503
Finite-difference component samples confirm the composed
gradient to 3.7 parts per million.

9
00:00:51,503 --> 00:00:56,612
The strongest shortcut still differentiates every
component, but freezes temperature inside buoyancy.

10
00:00:56,612 --> 00:01:05,180
At this strong setting it has 86 percent relative error
and wrong signs in 33 percent of the design field, while
the forward temperature gives no warning.

11
00:01:05,430 --> 00:01:14,567
A norm is not an outcome, so each gradient proposes the
same count and amplitude of positive and negative
raw-design changes and is judged by a fresh coupled solve.

12
00:01:14,567 --> 00:01:17,783
The composed choice wins all 3 tested action sizes.

13
00:01:17,783 --> 00:01:23,878
At the largest step it delivers 58 percent more realized
cooling under the same zero-sum raw-design rule.

14
00:01:24,128 --> 00:01:29,522
We froze the repeated procedure before storing these
trajectories, but the same operating point already had

15
00:01:29,522 --> 00:01:34,682
favorable one-step evidence, so this is follow-up rather
than an untouched independent confirmation.

16
00:01:34,682 --> 00:01:42,333
The protocol gives every branch the same start,
projected-volume target, eight update opportunities, and
true candidate-solve budget.

17
00:01:42,333 --> 00:01:52,599
The frozen eight-step endpoint has no winner because the
composed step-six candidate did not converge. Over the
shared first 5 accepted decisions, the descriptive

18
00:01:52,599 --> 00:02:00,502
reductions are 11.83, 5.16, and 4.71 percent; that common
prefix was examined after the failure and is not the
frozen endpoint.

19
00:02:00,502 --> 00:02:04,043
The failure is retained without parameter tuning or
selective rerun.

20
00:02:04,293 --> 00:02:13,883
This retrospective frozen extension retains every failure;
13 attempts overlap the earlier pilot and 35 cells had no
stored result when the design was frozen.

21
00:02:13,883 --> 00:02:20,873
Among 39 comparable cases, the exact action wins 35, the
shortcut wins 1, and 3 are ties.

22
00:02:20,873 --> 00:02:27,363
The post-freeze descriptive 95 percent seed-cluster
bootstrap interval has a lower endpoint of 81.1 percent;

23
00:02:27,363 --> 00:02:31,298
the other 9 attempts remain visible as noncomparable, not
deleted.

24
00:02:31,548 --> 00:02:39,373
The de Vahl Davis reference activates full nonlinear
Navier Stokes inertia, hot and cold side walls, and
insulated horizontal walls.

25
00:02:39,373 --> 00:02:46,943
At Rayleigh 1000 and 10000, all 6 Nusselt and
centerline-velocity metrics are within 1.2 percent of the
published reference.

26
00:02:46,943 --> 00:02:57,195
A separate 5 by 5 by 2 millimeter sealed-water example
maps every nondimensional group back to S I units and
preserves exactly 1 watt on the discretized chip.

27
00:02:57,195 --> 00:03:07,237
Only 3 of 6 planned layout and mesh solves converged; the
N equals 32 finned solve stalled, so its apparent
reduction is withheld rather than promoted as evidence.

28
00:03:07,237 --> 00:03:15,527
Even the converged baseline predicts a temperature above
water's liquid range, outside the constant-property model
used for this scaling exercise.

29
00:03:15,527 --> 00:03:21,878
The retained failure is a boundary on the dimensional
illustration, not a performance or equal-material
optimization claim.

30
00:03:22,128 --> 00:03:32,054
The loop-cut adjoint's exact equation residual is Phi
transpose g; normalizing it costs one V J P and retains
the objective direction spectral radius discards.

31
00:03:32,054 --> 00:03:39,171
Across 14 converged physical configurations, its log
correlation with measured error is 0.995.

32
00:03:39,171 --> 00:03:48,842
Across 2,377 synthetic fixed points, it is 0.989, versus
0.691 for spectral radius.

33
00:03:49,092 --> 00:03:59,332
The limit is explicit: correlation falls to 0.36 when the
loop repels, so the reusable PyTree utility provides no
universal threshold and never calls that regime safe.

34
00:03:59,332 --> 00:04:05,938
An upstream-ready Tesseract JAX issue and test plan are
prepared, but nothing will be submitted before publication
review.

35
00:04:06,188 --> 00:04:13,305
At the weaker-coupling topology-optimization start both
gradients can descend, which is precisely why the
strong-setting decision studies matter.

36
00:04:13,305 --> 00:04:19,273
The full composed run over 120 iterations lowers the chip
objective by 84.6 percent.

37
00:04:19,273 --> 00:04:24,474
It forms a branching conductor toward the cold sink while
preserving channels for buoyant coolant flow.

38
00:04:24,724 --> 00:04:34,442
Linux C I runs the tests and claim audit, while a separate
job rebuilds all four component images and serves three at
a time across the real derivative boundary.

39
00:04:34,442 --> 00:04:43,463
The August twenty-ninth release workflow records exact O C
I digests, checksums the paper and video, and refuses to
publish until anonymous pulls succeed.

40
00:04:43,463 --> 00:04:51,671
Coldplate is a two-way equilibrium whose composition
changes a measured engineering decision, with the evidence
and the failure modes attached.
